# .env.template — secrets template (values empty; never commit the filled .env)
# Copy to .env on-target and fill. .env is gitignored.
#
# Secrets are env-var-only and live in .env (gitignored), filled from this template.
# DO-NOT-COPY anti-example: any .mcp.json shipping plaintext tokens. Never do that.
#
# The Pilot ingests only local Claude Code jsonl — no API key is required to run it.
# This file is a forward-provision placeholder; add keys here only if a later pass needs them.
#
# OPTIONAL (cloud, EGRESS) — ONLY for scripts/fetch_usage_cloud.py, the opt-in
# Claude Enterprise Analytics fetcher. Leaving it empty keeps the agent fully
# air-gapped (the fetcher no-ops without it). This key is NOT used by the core
# extract/coordinate pipeline. Create it as the Enterprise Primary Owner at
# claude.ai > Organization settings > API (scope read:analytics).
ANALYTICS_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL (egress) — ONLY for scripts/count_tokens.py "exact" mode (estimate a prompt's
# INPUT tokens BEFORE sending, via POST /v1/messages/count_tokens). This is a regular
# Messages API key (x-api-key), NOT the read:analytics Analytics key above. Leaving it empty
# keeps count_tokens.py fully OFFLINE (it falls back to a local ~approx heuristic, no network).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
